{"entryId":"1426","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1426:1","sourceSha256":"d32f54b04ba56f54cbbd2f096c2175ba56409c25b441fd6611d6b421ed8f8548","englishSha256":"90ddd5d6d1f19b77d1a5488b11bac863f4f96f5978d9cbc54ad447be4b8798e3","citations":[{"id":"1426:1:citation-01","he":[0,82],"en":[0,23],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_39a.11"},"reference":"Kiddushin 39a:11","assessment":"The exact Bavli gives both sages and the two speech turns without assigning the requests to a named individual.","evidence":[{"reference":"Kiddushin 39a:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_39a.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1426:1:citation-02","he":[113,175],"en":[433,446],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_39a.12"},"reference":"Kiddushin 39a:12","assessment":"The second episode likewise keeps the speech turns unnamed. The immediately following argument identifies Rabbi Yoshiyah as the authority.","evidence":[{"reference":"Kiddushin 39a:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_39a.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1426:1:citation-03","he":[84,111],"en":[154,200],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Kiddushin_39a.11.2"},"reference":"Rashi on Kiddushin 39a:11:2","assessment":"The gloss is an exact near-verbatim agreement with Rashi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Kiddushin 39a:11:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Kiddushin_39a.11.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1426:1:citation-04","he":[177,211],"en":[345,399],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Kiddushin_39a.12.1"},"reference":"Rashi on Kiddushin 39a:12:1","assessment":"The wording of the second gloss agrees with Rashi’s explanation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Kiddushin 39a:12:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Kiddushin_39a.12.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,2,1,3],"holds":[{"raw"